# Otipi (SMS / OTP / email API for Israel)

- SDK: `npm install otipi`. `import { Otipi, OtipiError } from 'otipi'`; `const otipi = new Otipi(process.env.OTIPI_KEY!)`.
- Key: free `sk_test_` key at https://otipi.co.il/signup. Server environment only (`.env.local`). Never in client components, `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, `VITE_*` or git.
- Login is two server calls: `await otipi.otp.send({ to, app: 'MyApp' })`, then `const { valid, reason } = await otipi.otp.verify({ to, code })`. Do not generate or store codes yourself.
- Phones: Israeli mobiles in E.164 `+9725XXXXXXXX`. Normalize user input (`050-123-4567`) on the server: strip spaces/dashes, `0` prefix -> `+972`, check `/^\+9725\d{8}$/`.
- Next.js App Router: `lib/otipi.ts` with `import 'server-only'`; routes `app/api/otp/send/route.ts` and `app/api/otp/verify/route.ts`; a `'use client'` page that calls them. Example: https://github.com/otipi-il/otipi-node/tree/main/examples/nextjs-sms-login
- Errors: catch `OtipiError` and use `err.code`: `invalid_recipient` (400), `too_many_codes` / `rate_limited` (429), `free_test_sms_used`, `unauthorized`. `otp.verify` returns `{ valid: false, reason }` instead of throwing for a wrong code.
- Test mode: `sk_test_` messages reach nobody except the owner's numbers confirmed in the dashboard (**API keys > Your numbers for tests**) or with `otipi.testRecipients.add({ to })` + `.verify({ to, code })`; 5 free test SMS. `otp.send` returns `test_code` in test mode. Answers carry `test_delivery: "real" | "sandbox"`. Never show `test_code` to end users.
- Supabase phone auth and auth emails: no code needed. Copy the hook address and secret from the Otipi dashboard (page Connect) and add an HTTPS Send SMS hook (and Send Email hook) in Supabase Authentication > Hooks. Do not add an Authorization header: Otipi checks the Standard Webhooks signature. Client: `supabase.auth.signInWithOtp({ phone })`, then `supabase.auth.verifyOtp({ phone, token, type: 'sms' })`.
- Docs: https://otipi.co.il/en/docs · https://otipi.co.il/llms-full.txt · https://otipi.co.il/openapi.json
